1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,649
Citibank meant to wire 7.8 million

2
00:00:02,649 --> 00:00:05,064
dollars in interest for Revlon.

3
00:00:05,064 --> 00:00:05,687
Instead,

4
00:00:05,687 --> 00:00:08,804
it accidentally wired almost 900 million

5
00:00:08,804 --> 00:00:10,128
of its own money.

6
00:00:10,128 --> 00:00:12,465
Here is Exhibit Figure 1 from court.

7
00:00:12,465 --> 00:00:14,672
Three reviewers checked PRINCIPAL,

8
00:00:14,672 --> 00:00:16,620
but missed that FRONT and FUND

9
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:18,243
also had to be checked to

10
00:00:18,243 --> 00:00:19,152
stop the wire.

11
00:00:19,152 --> 00:00:21,609
Ten firms refused to return over

12
00:00:21,609 --> 00:00:23,144
500 million dollars.

13
00:00:23,144 --> 00:00:25,217
A trial judge let them keep

14
00:00:25,217 --> 00:00:27,366
it in 2021 before an appeals

15
00:00:27,366 --> 00:00:29,976
court reversed the ruling in 2022.

16
00:00:29,976 --> 00:00:31,864
Wall Street never forgot.

17
00:00:31,864 --> 00:00:33,223
By September 2026,

18
00:00:33,223 --> 00:00:36,621
erroneous payment clawback clauses sit inside

19
00:00:36,621 --> 00:00:39,792
88 percent of corporate credit agreements.

20
00:00:39,792 --> 00:00:42,342
Three human reviewers still missed a

21
00:00:42,342 --> 00:00:43,830
bad software default.

22
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,734
High-stakes systems need clearer screens,

23
00:00:46,734 --> 00:00:48,576
not just extra signatures.
